aeltra-distro-tools (1.14.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * distro-info: the package sources of a release come from here now.
    repository_sources() lays them out as <mirror>/<release>/
    <repository>/<arch>/<libc>/<pocket> from releases.json and
    mirrors.json, named <repository>-<pocket>, so no tool assembles
    archive URLs itself any more. A repository has the pockets main,
    tools and cross-tools, unless releases.json lists its own; one
    without a requested pocket is skipped for it, so a build may ask
    for every pocket. An unknown repository or pocket is an error.
    repository_names() and repository_pockets() are new as well, and
    "aeltra-distro-info repositories <release>" lists the names.
  * image-gen: a spec says which sources it is applied with, in a
    preamble before any package or script section: "core" and "main"
    always, plus what its @repositories and @pockets lines name. Each
    spec gets exactly these, whatever earlier specs used, and the
    lists are updated on the host, with the cache and credentials the
    host-side aept calls get. The sources are named
    <repository>-<pocket> instead of main, tools and cross-tools.
  * image-gen: every spec run is recorded in /var/lib/image-gen/sources
    in the image, and "cleanup" gives the finished image the union of
    the sources recorded there, so that whatever was installed can be
    kept up to date. It needs no release data for that. "cleanup
    --repo <name>" adds a repository of the release besides, with the
    pockets the image uses where it has them.
  * image-gen: --repo-base is gone; a repository is named, never given
    as a URL. build-essential declares its tools pockets with @pockets
    instead of a chroot script that wrote plain-http sources and ran
    "aept update" inside the image, where no credentials reach.
  * python3-aeltra-image-gen depends on python3-aeltra-distro-info,
    which it has imported all along.
  * Tests: distro-info and image-gen have pytest suites now. tox runs
    them as py3, and flake8 as lint.

